# What to focus on

## Next PR: `/resume` age column and the resume test record

Branch: `fix/resume-age-column`. FOLLOWUP_TASKS items 69 and 38.

The last plan (stream end, LLM wire, prompt caching and wizard wrapping) shipped in #63. It is kept in `docs/old/2026-10-18-llm-wire-streams-caching-TODO.md`.

Work in this order. Each step is one commit.

### 1. Keep the full age in `/resume` (69)

The session browser cuts titles at a fixed 40 columns (`tui/session_browser.go:24`). At 50 columns this leaves 5 columns for the age, so the select list cuts it ("just now" shows as "just").

- Add an opt-in `FitLabel bool` to `SelectListComponent` (`tui/selectlist.go`), next to `WrapDescriptions`. When set and the description does not fit, cut the label so the full description fits.
- The session browser turns it on. Other lists keep their current behavior, since lists with long descriptions (such as slash commands) should keep their labels.
- Test (failing first): in `session_browser_test.go`, a 40-character title with `LastActive` now, rendered at width 50. The line contains "just now" and is no wider than 50 columns.

### 2. Record a failing run for `TestPickResume_SkipsChildAndLoadsChildren` (38)

No code change.

- Remove the `l.Depth == 0` filter in `session.List` (`session/list.go:36`) for a moment, run the test and check that it fails.
- Put the filter back and check that it passes.
- Record the failing output in this PR's live-test doc in `docs/reviews/`.

### Then

- Remove items 69 and 38 from `docs/FOLLOWUP_TASKS.md`. Add a CHANGELOG Unreleased entry for 69.
- Run `go vet`, `go test`, `golangci-lint`. Update snapshots only if output changes on purpose.
- Live test the `/resume` list at 50 columns with the gohome-full-test skill.

